guide forever/reputation/zandalar-tribe
title Zandalar Tribe Reputation
category Reputation
folder Reputation · Raids and dungeons
levels 60-60
zone Stranglethorn Vale
keywords Zandalar Tribe, Yojamba Isle, Zul'Gurub, Vinchaxa, Rin'wosho the Trader, Zanza the Restless, Zandalar Honor Token, Hakkari Bijou, Zulian Coin, Razzashi Coin, Hakkari Coin, Gurubashi Coin, Primal Hakkari Idol, Paragons of Power, Zandalar Signet of Might, Zandalar Signet of Mojo, Zandalar Signet of Serenity, shoulder enchant, Savage Guard, Arcanum, class necklace, Hakkar
why Shoulder and head enchants, a class necklace upgraded at every standing, and Zul'Gurub's set pieces.
reward item 20077 20076 20078
reward text Your class's necklace at Friendly, upgraded at Honored, Revered and Exalted
reward text Zanza's head and leg enchants, from Friendly

# Built from Forever's data: the Zandalar Tribe quest rows (reputation from Forever's quest pages; the world
# database's standing gates: the class necklaces at Friendly, Honored, Revered and Exalted, Zanza's enchants from
# Friendly, the Savage Guard and Essence Mangoes from Honored, Zanza's Potent Potables from Revered, the Signets
# of the Zandalar at Exalted), the kill reputation and the standing each kill stops at (world database), the
# Zul'Gurub drop tables (each coin about 5% from the trolls, each bijou colour 2% to 3% from the trash, the Primal
# Hakkari Idol from Jin'do and Mandokir about 90%), Rin'wosho the Trader's shop with each recipe's standing and
# price (Forever's client item table), and the spawns of Yojamba Isle. Destroying a bijou at the Altar of Zanza
# pays 75 reputation and an Honor Token through a spell (Forever's client spell data); the quest pages show
# none. A full clear by the database's spawns is about 4,050 reputation: about 2,700 from trash that stops at
# 11,999 of 12,000 Honored, about 1,350 from bosses that count to Exalted. Neutral to Exalted is 42,000. No race gets a
# reputation bonus in Forever; the Legacy perk Diplomat adds up to 10%. Numbers below are without it.
# Zanza the Restless stands inside Zul'Gurub; his goals point at the raid's entrance, placed from the client's
# map table (the corpse point outside it).
# The Arcanums for the Savage Guard bind on pickup and the Librams do not (Forever's client item table); the
# Lorekeeper's libram quests 7483-7485 take the libram, a Pristine Black Diamond, 2 or 4 Large Brilliant Shards and
# Blood of Heroes, Skin of Shadow or Frayed Abomination Stitching (quest data).
# Formula: Magnificent Trollshine (Honored, 4g) is tied to the Zandalar in Forever's client, but no vendor in
# Forever's data sells it; the guide names Rin'wosho as the likely seller.
# INGAME: Is Zul'Gurub open? Blizzard's raid announcement for Forever names Barrow Deeps, Hyjal Summit and
# Onyxia's Lair; Zul'Gurub is in the client but not announced.
# INGAME: Does Rin'wosho the Trader sell Formula: Magnificent Trollshine at Honored?
# INGAME: Does Zul'Gurub trash stop at 11,999 of 12,000 Honored? Forever's world database says so; Classic players
# reported it counting to 20,999 of 21,000 Revered.

step Yojamba Isle
  tip Yojamba Isle is the small island off the north-west coast of Stranglethorn Vale, west of the Zuuldaia Ruins: swim over from the coast. Everyone starts Neutral with the Zandalar Tribe. Vinchaxa takes coins and bijous, Rin'wosho the Trader sells the recipes and trades Honor Tokens, and Jin'rokh, Al'tabim, Maywiki and Falthir hand out the class necklaces and the set pieces. Almost all Zandalar reputation comes from Zul'Gurub, a 20-player raid, and Zul'Gurub is not among the first raids Blizzard has announced for Forever: until it opens there is no Zandalar reputation to earn, and no coins or bijous on the auction house either. Once it is open, the only solo way is buying coins and bijous on the auction house (75 per bijou, 25 per set of three coins). The Legacy perk Diplomat adds up to 10% to every gain; the numbers in this guide are without it.
  accept 8240                         -- Vinchaxa: A Bijou for Zanza

step Zul'Gurub to Friendly
  tip Zul'Gurub is the troll city in the north-east of Stranglethorn Vale: a 20-player raid. Trash pays 3 to 5 each until 11,999 of 12,000 Honored, one point short of Revered; the Speakers 15, Ohgan 15, the Edge of Madness boss 25, Gahz'ranka and the five High Priests 100, Bloodlord Mandokir and Jin'do 200 and Hakkar 400, all the way to Exalted. A full clear is about 4,050: one clear reaches Friendly (3,000). Loot every coin, bijou, Primal Hakkari Idol, Channeler's Head and Primal Hakkari set piece. Coins and bijous pay the same at any standing: save them until the trash stops counting, except one bijou for A Bijou for Zanza.
  collect 19707 optional              -- Red Hakkari Bijou; any of the nine colours does
  rep 270 Friendly

step A Bijou for Zanza
  tip Destroy one bijou at the Altar of Zanza, the stone altar on the west side of Yojamba Isle (right-click the bijou there), then tell Vinchaxa: 150 reputation and an extra Zandalar Honor Token, once. From then on every bijou you destroy at the altar pays 75 reputation and a token, and every set of three coins Vinchaxa takes pays 25 and a token. They never stop counting.
  turnin 8240 optional                -- Vinchaxa: 150

step Friendly: your class necklace
  tip At Friendly your class's trainer on the isle gives a necklace for free (100 reputation); the same NPC upgrades it at Honored, Revered and Exalted (100 each) with no raid item needed. Friendly also opens Rin'wosho's first recipes (Pattern: Bloodvine Boots, Primal Batskin Bracers, Plans: Bloodsoul Gauntlets, Darksoul Shoulders, Schematic: Bloodvine Lens, Recipe: Greater Dreamless Sleep, 5g each; Formula: Brilliant Mana Oil, 4g) and the Paragons of Power bracers (150 for the Primal Hakkari bracer token of your class).
  accept 8041 optional only Warrior   -- Jin'rokh the Breaker: Strength of Mugamba, Friendly
  turnin 8041 optional only Warrior   -- 100
